    "attributionDetail": "Owner-selected; identity and reuse evidence have NOT been newly verified. Photograph of a ranger and children gathered around an actual shallow sandy tidepool, with water, rock and seaweed. People dominate the composition, but visible physical shore activity and native named-place description establish a surrounding-environment record. Not an underwater dive-site photograph. Identity: Native item explicitly names Leo Carrillo State Park and depicts tidepool shore activity. Inventory is named Leo Carrillo State Beach; its SSI source describes Carrillo West Cove. Exact photographed cove and inventory pin are not established. Limitations: {\"relationship\": \"Native item explicitly names Leo Carrillo State Park and depicts tidepool shore activity. Inventory is named Leo Carrillo State Beach; its SSI source describes Carrillo West Cove. Exact photographed cove and inventory pin are not established.\", \"holds\": [\"Quality/composition: people dominate; limited wider shoreline context and no hero-image suitability asserted.\", \"Geography: exact cove, dive entry and inventory coordinate unverified; named surrounding setting only.\", \"Privacy/publication: identifiable people including apparent minors; no model release asserted. Human publication and privacy review required.\", \"Historical imagery: 2005 date; no present-day condition or access assurance.\", \"No certified site coverage, main-photo assignment or production publication is authorized.\"], \"status\": \"QUALITY_GEOGRAPHY_PRIVACY_HELD_SURROUNDING_ENVIRONMENT_RECORD\"}  Resized and JPEG re-encoded; hero may be cropped."
